From: aliosa27 <aliosa27@aliosa27.me>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:38:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/27] UART AT input: echo, line editing, run on Enter

libatcmd's UART front end treats each burst of input ending in a 5-tick gap
as one command and echoes nothing, so typing in a terminal sent one-letter
commands. Replace it: binary bursts (XMODEM for AT+FWUPG) and whole lines
sent at once pass through as before; typed input is echoed, Backspace/DEL
edit it, and CR or LF runs the line.
